  so energy is a little trickier both  classical and quantum energies are  constant over time  that's right but the magnitude differs  by this term you might remember that  this term is what we called the zero  point energy of the quantum harmonic  oscillator  which is a purely quantum phenomenon  for classical oscillators the magnitude  of alpha zero is much much larger  than the zero point energy which means  that to a very good approximation  the energy in a quantum coherent state  is also the same  as the classical energy putting all of  this together  the coherent states of a quantum  harmonic oscillator  are the quantum states that most closely  follow the motion of a classical  particle  in a harmonic oscillator and this is a  reason why coherent states are also  called  quasi-classical states coherent states  also called quasi-classical states are  what we need to make  a quantum harmonic oscillator actually  oscillate  to see this more explicitly you should  check out our video on the wave  functions of the coherent states  and as always if you liked the video  please subscribe
 

